window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-ryuuen-kakeru"]=[{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 4  named before he is seen the volume names him for the first time in ichinose s warning   someone named ryuuen kun masterminded that one    the earlier class b class c dispute  and the sudou setup behind this case  as ichinose describes him   he doesn t hesitate to hurt other people for the sake of his own interests  he s a formidable opponent  she adds that he  hasn t seen any reason to reveal himself just yet  which is why ayanokoji does not know the name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.4: named before he is seen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.241<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The volume names him for the first time in Ichinose’s warning: &quot;Someone named Ryuuen-kun masterminded that one.&quot; — the earlier Class B–Class C dispute, and the Sudou setup behind this case.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> As Ichinose describes him: &quot;He doesn’t hesitate to hurt other people for the sake of his own interests. He’s a formidable opponent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She adds that he &quot;hasn’t seen any reason to reveal himself just yet,&quot; which is why Ayanokōji does not know the name.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.6: the boy in the corridor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 6  the boy in the corridor he stops in front of ayanokoji and horikita in the corridor   black hair worn long  about ayanokoji s height  a wide grin the page calls ominous  never fully turning to face them  the scene does not name him   setting up a camera  you really did something funny  huh   next time  i ll be your opponent  i look forward to it  he walks on without answering horikita s  and you are  ayanokoji s closing inventory names the encounter   we d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as ryuuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.6: the boy in the corridor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.254–255<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He stops in front of Ayanokōji and Horikita in the corridor — black hair worn long, about Ayanokōji’s height, a wide grin the page calls ominous, never fully turning to face them. The scene does not name him.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Setting up a camera? You really did something funny, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Next time, I’ll be your opponent. I look forward to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He walks on without answering Horikita’s &quot;And you are?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ayanokōji’s closing inventory names the encounter: &quot;We’d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as Ryuuen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.4: named before he is seen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  3 2  the beach at zero holds court on the class c beach in swimwear   tanned  laid back in his chair  flashing white teeth   just as you see  we re enjoying our summer vacation   hmm  well  i didn t make a precise calculation  pours his remaining water on the sand  almost in provocation  while ishizaki fetches another bottle   class d  the lowest of all  has to put up with starvation  heat  and futility just to save a measly 100 or 200 class points  it makes me laugh   i said to bring me cold water  this water s warm   ryuuen s pupils were just like those of a snake    the returned bottle comes back in ishizaki s face   cooperation  don t make me laugh  people betray each other with ease  people lie  relationships built on trust just aren t viable  you can only trust yourself   i absolutely loathe hard work  patience  saving  you must be joking   ah  she ran out of here rather suddenly  she went looking for help from another class in the end  pathetic girl  admits her light punishment was a slap   he gestures it   and offers forgiveness only on his terms   if she grovels on the ground  i ll forgive her  i ve a tolerant heart   another boy defied me as well  so i had him driven out  i heard he didn t die  so he s probably off somewhere eating grass and insects to survive  spent the entire three hundred point budget on day one    yes  as you said  i used all of our points    so there is nothing left to penalize   ha ha ha  what should i do  i wonder  well  i suppose that plain  ordinary people can only engage in plain  ordinary thinking  calls her by her first name against her refusal  and answers her disgust while touching himself under the bathing suit   see you later  suzune   well  i rather like forceful women  i ll make you submit to me eventually  when that time comes  it will be the ultimate pleasure  treats his fetch boy as furniture   the warm bottle is thrown back at him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: the beach at zero<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.109–115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Holds court on the Class C beach in swimwear — tanned, laid back in his chair, flashing white teeth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ishizaki-daichi\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Just as you see. We&#x27;re enjoying our summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm. Well, I didn&#x27;t make a precise calculation,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Class D, the lowest of all, has to put up with starvation, heat, and futility just to save a measly 100 or 200 class points. It makes me laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pours his remaining water on the sand “almost in provocation” while Ishizaki fetches another bottle.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I said to bring me cold water. This water&#x27;s warm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Ryuuen&#x27;s pupils were just like those of a snake.” — the returned bottle comes back in Ishizaki&#x27;s face.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cooperation? Don&#x27;t make me laugh. People betray each other with ease. People lie. Relationships built on trust just aren&#x27;t viable. You can only trust yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I absolutely loathe hard work. Patience? Saving? You must be joking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. She ran out of here rather suddenly. She went looking for help from another class in the end? Pathetic girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Admits her light punishment was a slap — he gestures it — and offers forgiveness only on his terms: “If she grovels on the ground, I&#x27;ll forgive her. I&#x27;ve a tolerant heart.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Another boy defied me as well, so I had him driven out. I heard he didn&#x27;t die, so he&#x27;s probably off somewhere eating grass and insects to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Spent the entire three-hundred-point budget on day one — “Yes, as you said. I used all of our points.” — so there is nothing left to penalize.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha ha. What should I do, I wonder? Well, I suppose that plain, ordinary people can only engage in plain, ordinary thinking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Calls her by her first name against her refusal, and answers her disgust while touching himself under the bathing suit.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I rather like forceful women. I&#x27;ll make you submit to me eventually. When that time comes, it will be the ultimate pleasure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Treats his fetch-boy as furniture — the warm bottle is thrown back at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p221-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.9: collecting the card<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p221-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 6  6 9  collecting the card answers ibuki s flashlight signal in the wet woods to collect what his operation stole  his spy since the test began   she reports to him over the transceiver and hands the card over   yo  excellent work  ibuki  you did well   naturally  if you hadn t made any mistakes until now  i wouldn t have had to risk coming over here   so  where s the card  checks the engraved name under his flashlight and calls katsuragi out of the shadows to confirm it   you come over here and confirm it  too  that was your condition  remember  relax  it s dark out  and this weather is horrible  there shouldn t be anyone here  it s great to be cautious  but don t waste time  holds her stolen leader card under the flashlight  engraved name up   are you convinced now  untagged  it follows the card and the inspection  so it is recorded as his   don t sit there and think about it forever  the situation is black and white  so make your decision  you re already halfway there  don t do something as stupid as pulling out here  presses the offer with sakayanagi s faction rumor   the student council failure   framed as katsuragi s chance   if this wasn t an honorable deed  then what are you going to do  did you know that sakayanagi s faction has dominated ever since rumors spread that you failed to get on the student council despite your best efforts  this might be your chance  right   class a maintains its position by forming alliances  if you can form those  even those who have double crossed you will return under your wing  won t they  or you could make me your enemy  i suppose  if you do  i wonder what would happen   that s good  you ve exercised sound judgment   to form an alliance  with class a  takes his handshake on the class a alliance after the pressure   the narration calls it a contract with the devil   i have that covered  of course  he will have no choice but to honor his promise  the answer to ibuki s renege question is untagged  it is his  against her doubt  lays out the contract s terms to ibuki with a creepy smile   the page never quotes them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.9: collecting the card<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.221–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Answers Ibuki’s flashlight signal in the wet woods to collect what his operation stole.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yo. Excellent work, Ibuki. You did well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Naturally? If you hadn’t made any mistakes until now, I wouldn’t have had to risk coming over here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, where’s the card?”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> His spy since the test began — she reports to him over the transceiver and hands the card over.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Checks the engraved name under his flashlight and calls Katsuragi out of the shadows to confirm it.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You come over here and confirm it, too. That was your condition, remember? Relax, it’s dark out, and this weather is horrible. There shouldn’t be anyone here. It’s great to be cautious, but don’t waste time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Holds her stolen leader card under the flashlight, engraved name up.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you convinced now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Untagged; it follows the card and the inspection, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t sit there and think about it forever. The situation is black-and-white, so make your decision. You’re already halfway there. Don’t do something as stupid as pulling out here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Presses the offer with Sakayanagi’s faction rumor — the student-council failure — framed as Katsuragi’s chance.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If this wasn’t an honorable deed, then what are you going to do? Did you know that Sakayanagi’s faction has dominated ever since rumors spread that you failed to get on the student council despite your best efforts? This might be your chance, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class A maintains its position by forming alliances. If you can form those, even those who have double-crossed you will return under your wing, won’t they? Or you could make me your enemy, I suppose? If you do, I wonder what would happen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s good. You’ve exercised sound judgment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To form an alliance. With Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Takes his handshake on the Class A alliance after the pressure — the narration calls it a contract with the devil.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have that covered, of course. He will have no choice but to honor his promise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The answer to Ibuki’s renege question is untagged; it is his, against her doubt.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lays out the contract’s terms to Ibuki with a creepy smile — the page never quotes them.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the beach at zero<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p241-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the lone Class C<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p241-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  the lone class c the only class c student left on the beach comes over to provoke the class d trio  hears the results in his face  and later turns up in the lounge retelling as the variable with the most information   oh  hey there  sycophants  what happened to suzune   i know you ve been chasing suzune s ass  we were together before  you know  drains his cup  then crushes it and throws it at ayanokoji s feet   throw that away for me   what a stupid thing to say  huh  pick up your own trash  jerk   but picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage   calm down  sudou kun  here  i ll throw it away   who are you  more importantly  where s suzune  i ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom   the next time you say something stupid  i ll kill you  sudou growled   what are you doing  and  huh  what s with you  getting all excited by yourself  huh  run untagged around sudou s tagged threat and are left out as chapter attribution gaps   horikita san retired yesterday  she s not here   retired  suzune  she doesn t seem like that kind of girl   i thought you retired  ryuuen kun  and the interrupted reply  that s  are left out as chapter attribution gaps  the broken three quarter mark is kept as printed   that s what we should be saying to you class c people  you used up all of your points  right  don t make us laugh   ha  i m jealous of the nerve of you small fry  how you can be satisfied with that amount of points   that s right  i wrote it on the paper  didn t i  the name of class d s leader   also  those guys in a and b wrote the same thing  too  do you know what this means  the page s own reading of the reveal  if the name holds  class d is hit with penalties and loses 100 points   it doesn t really matter whatever you say  class c is still going to stay at zero points  runs untagged between ryuuen s taunts and is left out as a chapter attribution gap   zero  can only watch in silence as the class d trio heads for the boat with sudou s gesture in the air  read as the variable with more information than himself   the identities of all the leaders in hand  classes a and c were connected behind the scenes  class c sacrificed its own points and bought whatever class a needed  and by taking all of c s tools class a spent the week without using any points   ibuki s evidence went to someone in class a  ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact  ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation   no one else controlled it  and his mistake was trusting no one  the test in one line  class a failed on its internal rift  class b ran defense only and paid for believing kaneda  class c sent spies and negotiated with a  and class d avoided damage because he had been appointed the leader  named the number one enemy   spies for the leaders  identities plus whatever the class a negotiations bought","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the lone Class C<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.241–257<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The only Class C student left on the beach comes over to provoke the Class D trio, hears the results in his face, and later turns up in the lounge retelling as the variable with the most information.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, hey there, sycophants. What happened to Suzune?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I know you’ve been chasing Suzune’s ass. We were together before, you know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Throw that away for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>23 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Drains his cup, then crushes it and throws it at Ayanokōji’s feet.<span class=\"pg\">p.241–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a stupid thing to say. Huh? Pick up your own trash, jerk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, Sudou-kun. Here, I’ll throw it away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who are you? More importantly, where’s Suzune? I’ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next time you say something stupid, I’ll kill you,” Sudou growled.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “What are you doing?” and “Huh? What’s with you? Getting all excited by yourself, huh?” run untagged around Sudou’s tagged threat and are left out as chapter attribution gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san retired yesterday. She’s not here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Retired? Suzune? She doesn’t seem like that kind of girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I thought you retired, Ryuuen-kun.” and the interrupted reply “That’s¾” are left out as chapter attribution gaps; the broken three-quarter mark is kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what we should be saying to you Class C people. You used up all of your points, right? Don’t make us laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha. I’m jealous of the nerve of you small fry. How you can be satisfied with that amount of points…”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. I wrote it on the paper, didn’t I? The name of Class D’s leader.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, those guys in A and B wrote the same thing, too. Do you know what this means?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The page’s own reading of the reveal: if the name holds, Class D is hit with penalties and loses 100 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “It doesn’t really matter whatever you say; Class C is still going to stay at zero points.” runs untagged between Ryuuen’s taunts and is left out as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Zero?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Can only watch in silence as the Class D trio heads for the boat with Sudou’s gesture in the air.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Read as the variable with more information than himself — the identities of all the leaders in hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Classes A and C were connected behind the scenes: Class C sacrificed its own points and bought whatever Class A needed, and by taking all of C’s tools Class A spent the week without using any points — Ibuki’s evidence went to someone in Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact; Ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation — no one else controlled it, and his mistake was trusting no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The test in one line: Class A failed on its internal rift, Class B ran defense-only and paid for believing Kaneda, Class C sent spies and negotiated with A, and Class D avoided damage because he had been appointed the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Named the number one enemy — spies for the leaders’ identities plus whatever the Class A negotiations bought.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p221-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.9: collecting the card<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2  2 5  the walk through provocation arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys  sizes up the pond  and picks a fight with katsuragi   well  well  so many fish in this pond  i ve come to take a look for myself   unfortunately  it looks like i m with you   to katsuragi s question whether he belongs to the meeting   how about you put on a little show for me  what do you think of beauty and the beast   looking at both horikita and katsuragi  then letting out a demented little chuckle   academic ability  how droll  that kind of thing is meaningless   hmm  awful attitude  what in the world are you talking about  i can t possibly imagine  can you perhaps tell me how i am  in fact  awful  gestured to his crew as if to ask whether katsuragi s argument was believable   their response mechanical  his three followers wear terrified looks and move docile    more like a king and his servants  the academic society argument ends in a cold stalemate  she flips her hair and turns her back on him to go inside","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.57–60<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys, sizes up the pond, and picks a fight with Katsuragi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, well. So many fish in this pond. I’ve come to take a look for myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Unfortunately, it looks like I’m with you.” (to Katsuragi’s question whether he belongs to the meeting)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How about you put on a little show for me? What do you think of Beauty and the Beast?” (looking at both Horikita and Katsuragi, then letting out a demented little chuckle)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Academic ability? How droll. That kind of thing is meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm? Awful attitude? What in the world are you talking about? I can’t possibly imagine. Can you perhaps tell me how I am, in fact, awful?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gestured to his crew as if to ask whether Katsuragi’s argument was believable; “their response mechanical.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His three followers wear terrified looks and move docile — “more like a king and his servants.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The academic-society argument ends in a cold stalemate.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She flips her hair and turns her back on him to go inside.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  3 0  the cafe provocation walks into blue ocean with ibuki mid horikita briefing  straddles a vacant seat  and spends the coffee working the island result until he leaves with his lackey   nice weather  eh suzune  you having breakfast with this clingy beta male   you should have received the message already  what were the results  were you chosen as the vip   i suppose you wouldn t give anything away  but that doesn t matter  according to my information  there s no way that your farcical bumbling on the island should ve led to victory  said ryuuen   yesterday  it seemed katsuragi was rather cautious of you  he said   heh  well  i won t deny that  i came here to measure your abilities for myself  he answered   katsuragi and i think differently  when i m dealing with someone  i like to keep an eye on them   i m remembering the test on the island  the result  the process that led to it  there are only certain types of people who would ve been able to conceptualize and execute a plan like that  a girl like you is far too serious minded to have come up with it  reasoned ryuuen   katsuragi probably didn t know   his read on who grasped the points flow   at the end of the test  i wrote down your name as leader  but that was wrong  there s just one reason why that was wrong  your class leader changed right before the test ended  the only explanation  mused ryuuen   ah  however  katsuragi thinks you planned the whole thing  but was that really the case  in my opinion  you becoming the leader and then retiring were both unexpected  besides  i had my own strategy in place  i had ibuki infiltrate your class to find out the leader s identity  you did nothing to counter that strategy at first  said ryuuen   the key question is who replaced you as leader  personally  i think the second leader was pulling your strings from behind the scenes during the entire test  speaks to horikita but watches ayanokoji the whole time    if i appeared shaken for even an instant  he d pounce   well  i suppose that s expected of a clingy tagalong   that guy with you is considerably smart  despite that  he hasn t achieved anything significant  or gotten high grades  he has some excellent qualities  though i have my doubts  said ryuuen   i see your point  i never imagined you d trip me up  i ll admit it  the results of the test shocked me  answered ryuuen   well  that s too bad  i love surprise attacks  foul play  and subterfuge  that level of strategy was totally unexpected  but your victory high will soon come to an end  whether it s you  suzune  or someone pulling the strings behind the scenes  you re stupid  you ve already made your best move  class d is one or two steps behind the other classes in points  the challenge will only heat up from here  you already played your trump card during the survival test  when the game was just getting started  you couldn t see what was in front of or behind you  i don t think you ll find this round as easy as last time  tell that to whoever helped you ace the test  warned ryuuen   what can i say  i m quite merciful  snaps a photo of horikita without asking  studies the sour expression  and pockets the phone satisfied   someone in class d other than you is quite clever  there s no mistake about that  he said   a conversation reveals many subtle things  i m glad i could talk with you  suzune  it s a game to me  i ll discover who among you is making moves behind the scenes  everyone  including your clingy friend here  is a target  said ryuuen   i already know their abilities  to some extent  neither katsuragi nor ichinose is my enemy  if i wanted to crush them  i could do it any time   i m saving her for the final course  it d be a waste to eat her now  let s go  ibuki  ryuuen stood and left with his lackey   on sakayanagi  the whole visit is reconnaissance  measure horikita  float the hidden second leader theory  and leave without confirming anything   narration says he only wanted to chat and pass the time amusing himself  the target of the visit  he needles her  photographs her  and walks off still doubting her  brings her as the visible lackey and cuts her off when she would snap back  sizes him up as smart but inert and keeps him in the target set without ever addressing him directly  the rival whose caution and island read he quotes back at horikita  saved  for the final course    he will not spend her now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.68–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into Blue Ocean with Ibuki mid-Horikita-briefing, straddles a vacant seat, and spends the coffee working the island result until he leaves with his lackey.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Nice weather, eh Suzune? You having breakfast with this clingy beta male?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You should have received the message already. What were the results? Were you chosen as the VIP?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I suppose you wouldn’t give anything away, but that doesn’t matter. According to my information, there’s no way that your farcical bumbling on the island should’ve led to victory,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yesterday, it seemed Katsuragi was rather cautious of you,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. Well, I won’t deny that. I came here to measure your abilities for myself,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi and I think differently. When I’m dealing with someone, I like to keep an eye on them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m remembering the test on the island. The result. The process that led to it. There are only certain types of people who would’ve been able to conceptualize and execute a plan like that. A girl like you is far too serious-minded to have come up with it,” reasoned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi probably didn’t know.” (his read on who grasped the points flow)<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At the end of the test, I wrote down your name as leader, but that was wrong. There’s just one reason why that was wrong: Your class leader changed right before the test ended. The only explanation,” mused Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. However, Katsuragi thinks you planned the whole thing. But was that really the case? In my opinion, you becoming the leader and then retiring were both unexpected. Besides, I had my own strategy in place. I had Ibuki infiltrate your class to find out the leader’s identity. You did nothing to counter that strategy at first,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The key question is who replaced you as leader. Personally, I think the second leader was pulling your strings from behind the scenes during the entire test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Speaks to Horikita but watches Ayanokōji the whole time — “If I appeared shaken for even an instant, he’d pounce.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose that’s expected of a clingy tagalong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That guy with you is considerably smart. Despite that, he hasn’t achieved anything significant, or gotten high grades. He has some excellent qualities, though I have my doubts,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see your point. I never imagined you’d trip me up. I’ll admit it. The results of the test shocked me,” answered Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s too bad. I love surprise attacks, foul play, and subterfuge. That level of strategy was totally unexpected, but your victory high will soon come to an end. Whether it’s you, Suzune, or someone pulling the strings behind the scenes, you’re stupid. You’ve already made your best move. Class D is one or two steps behind the other classes in points. The challenge will only heat up from here. You already played your trump card during the survival test, when the game was just getting started. You couldn’t see what was in front of or behind you. I don’t think you’ll find this round as easy as last time. Tell that to whoever helped you ace the test,” warned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What can I say? I’m quite merciful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snaps a photo of Horikita without asking, studies the sour expression, and pockets the phone satisfied.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone in Class D other than you is quite clever. There’s no mistake about that,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A conversation reveals many subtle things. I’m glad I could talk with you, Suzune. It’s a game to me. I’ll discover who among you is making moves behind the scenes. Everyone, including your clingy friend here, is a target,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I already know their abilities, to some extent. Neither Katsuragi nor Ichinose is my enemy. If I wanted to crush them, I could do it any time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m saving her for the final course. It’d be a waste to eat her now. Let’s go, Ibuki.” Ryuuen stood and left with his lackey. (on Sakayanagi)<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The whole visit is reconnaissance: measure Horikita, float the hidden-second-leader theory, and leave without confirming anything — narration says he only wanted to chat and pass the time amusing himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The target of the visit; he needles her, photographs her, and walks off still doubting her.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Brings her as the visible lackey and cuts her off when she would snap back.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sizes him up as smart-but-inert and keeps him in the target set without ever addressing him directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.68, 73–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The rival whose caution and island read he quotes back at Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.70, 72, 75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Saved “for the final course” — he will not spend her now.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hoshinomiya-chie katsuragi-kouhei ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  named twice  absent both times two second half mentions   the kouenji shock list and the teachers  dragon roster talk   katsuragi  ryuuen  and ichinose would all be surprised by this    grouped with them as a leader who had not imagined an early traitor  hoshinomiya s class c complaint   if we evaluated the class   c students properly  another student should ve been placed into dragon  but they threw ryuuen in there  the teacher who thinks the dragon pick was a class c evaluation failure  the other surprised leader on the same line  the third name on the surprise list","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.115, p.123<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two second-half mentions — the Kouenji shock list and the teachers’ Dragon roster talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Katsuragi, Ryuuen, and Ichinose would all be surprised by this” — grouped with them as a leader who had not imagined an early traitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Hoshinomiya’s Class C complaint: “If we evaluated the Class … C students properly, another student should’ve been placed into Dragon. But they threw Ryuuen in there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122-123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The teacher who thinks the Dragon pick was a Class C evaluation failure.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The other surprised leader on the same line.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The third name on the surprise list.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 4  4 0  the shade meeting and the planted phone he drops into horikita and ayanokoji s shade conversation  claims class c can win by rule logic  and leaves a silent recording phone under his own chair   hey  you two  having yourselves a nice date in the shade  let me in on the fun   that s for me to decide  well then  have you decided how to find the vip  he asked   i ve already started to discover the vip s identity  would you believe me if i told you that   well  you re right that i m not a professional friend collector  but making friends has nothing to do with whether or not i can gather information   unfortunately for you  i ve already gotten a handle on the fundamentals of this test  depending on how things go  class c will win by an overwhelming majority   it s an extremely simple matter  all you need to do is find out what   class the vip is from  then  your next move is to analyze the group  said ryuuen   you just have to make sure it s a situation where someone can t lie  he said   i take everyone s cell phones  so if someone lies to me  all i have to do is check everyone s email  one by one  said ryuuen   it s not really a problem at all  actually  i m here because it s not a problem  do you get what i mean  brute force phone seizure as a class c method   no complaints means consent  narration reads it as operating within the rules and as three vips already identified   looks like you finally understand   maybe i m just playing around   now  then  suppose i m about to reach checkmate  he said   i don t think about it at all  i don t really care about small fry  see you again  suzune  dismisses the monkey group early end as small fry  leaves  a silent phone set to record audio stays under his chair with the chat line  sorry for yesterday  parting  see you again  suzune    first name basis  reported","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.128–131<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He drops into Horikita and Ayanokōji’s shade conversation, claims Class C can win by rule-logic, and leaves a silent recording phone under his own chair.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, you two. Having yourselves a nice date in the shade? Let me in on the fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s for me to decide. Well then, have you decided how to find the VIP?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve already started to discover the VIP’s identity. Would you believe me if I told you that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, you’re right that I’m not a professional friend-collector, but making friends has nothing to do with whether or not I can gather information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately for you, I’ve already gotten a handle on the fundamentals of this test. Depending on how things go, Class C will win by an overwhelming majority.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s an extremely simple matter. All you need to do is find out what … class the VIP is from. Then, your next move is to analyze the group,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just have to make sure it’s a situation where someone can’t lie,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I take everyone’s cell phones. So if someone lies to me, all I have to do is check everyone’s email, one by one,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not really a problem at all, actually. I’m here because it’s not a problem. Do you get what I mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Brute-force phone seizure as a Class C method — no complaints means consent; narration reads it as operating within the rules and as three VIPs already identified.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you finally understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe I’m just playing around?”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now, then. Suppose I’m about to reach checkmate?” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think about it at all. I don’t really care about small fry. See you again, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Dismisses the Monkey-group early end as small fry.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Leaves; a silent phone set to record audio stays under his chair with the chat line “Sorry for yesterday!”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Parting “See you again, Suzune” — first-name basis, reported.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 5  5 0  the frontal assault still running named in the final day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate   united frontal assault against katsuragi s fortress  the two strategies ichinose has not answered  the chapter opens between them  still the fear she won t detail under listener risk at the 5 1 meet  no scene presence in this half  the row records the opening status line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the final-day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate — united frontal assault against Katsuragi’s fortress.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The two strategies Ichinose has not answered; the chapter opens between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Still the fear she won’t detail under listener risk at the 5.1 meet.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence in this half; the row records the opening status line.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the sixth guest<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 5  5 3  the sixth guest invited as the deliberate sixth seat  slams a chair beside horikita  names kushida as dragon vip from her body language  shows the class a vip list  claims the four email timing  and declares horikita his next target  the whole set piece is aimed at her   teasing  the reveal   you re my next target  tear you to shreds  both in mind and body   i thought i d enjoy finding out the results with you all  thanks so much for gathering in such an easy to find place  he said mockingly   anyway  suzune  you ve got a rather large group with you  have you grown more sociable  muttered ryuuen  looking out at the other four people gathered around the table and ignoring sudou completely  ignored on arrival  sudou s chide about the last results is brushed into the kushida play   i didn t think you actually had any friends  ryuuen teased   the results will be announced any minute now  are you expecting any results  he asked   heh  i wouldn t be here if i wasn t  looks like the same crowd as the last time  replied ryuuen   stop it  suzune  you know if you get carried away now  you ll just be embarrassed later  i already know our group s vip  said ryuuen   there s no need to wait for the announcement  want me to tell you who the dragon group vip is  he asked   if you could only understand the depth of my mercy  you d be moved  so moved that you ll get wet between your thighs  ryuuen laughed  as though such vulgar language was funny   kushida kikyou  the name dropped cold   known since the second day of the test   i m sorry  but i ve known kushida was the vip since the second day of the test  ryuuen said   i just felt so sorry for you  you were oh so incredibly confident in your victory that you looked down on others  you were desperate to get your stories straight  assuming no one would get the answer right  that s why i went along with it until the end  hirata s  how did you figure it out  carries curiosity and fear  the answer names horikita  not him   unfortunately  the answer to that  well  it involves you  suzune  answered ryuuen   i figured it out because of your body  the movements of your eyes and mouth  your breathing  your behavior  your tone  everything about you told me that you were lying  continued ryuuen in an eerie voice  body language read of horikita s lie   the method that beat the vip secret   jokes  if it s a joke  then how do i know the truth   i understand how you feel  you don t want to admit that you re the most incompetent person in the group  but don t beat yourself up  suzune  you merely chose the wrong opponent  besides  this exam was supposed to be pure chaos  at any rate  class a is in for an especially rude awakening  relax   you ll understand soon enough  the four simultaneous betrayal emails   rat  horse  monkey  rooster answered correctly  he played a major part  class a vip list on his screen for rat  rooster and pig   isn t this great  suzune  thanks to your blunder  the dragon group managed to clear this test with outcome  1  because of that  all the classes should receive a boost in points  ryuuen crowed  he clapped his hands and wore a satisfied grin   if you beg for it  i ll tell you the answer  how about it  he asked   ooh  that look you have  it s pretty sexy   i made some adjustments and arrived at the root of the test  then  i just focused on the class a students  he said  cleared without targeting classes b or d at all   the class a vip harvest on one screen   i m sorry to tell you  suzune  but you re my next target  i m going after you with everything i ve got  i won t stop until i tear you to shreds  both in mind and body   i m looking forward to the second semester  said ryuuen  walks away with his payback for the island   the threat ayanokoji turns into quiet excitement  the defensive vote he bent to 1    named in ayanokoji s explanation of dragon outcome  1","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3: the sixth guest<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.237–243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Invited as the deliberate sixth seat, slams a chair beside Horikita, names Kushida as Dragon VIP from her body language, shows the Class A VIP list, claims the four-email timing, and declares Horikita his next target.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I thought I’d enjoy finding out the results with you all. Thanks so much for gathering in such an easy-to-find place,” he said mockingly.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Anyway, Suzune, you’ve got a rather large group with you. Have you grown more sociable?” muttered Ryuuen, looking out at the other four people gathered around the table and ignoring Sudou completely.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I didn’t think you actually had any friends,” Ryuuen teased.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The whole set piece is aimed at her — teasing, the reveal, “you’re my next target… tear you to shreds, both in mind and body.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Ignored on arrival; Sudou’s chide about the last results is brushed into the Kushida play.<span class=\"pg\">p.238-239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The results will be announced any minute now. Are you expecting any results?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. I wouldn’t be here if I wasn’t. Looks like the same crowd as the last time,” replied Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop it, Suzune. You know if you get carried away now, you’ll just be embarrassed later. I already know our group’s VIP,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need to wait for the announcement. Want me to tell you who the Dragon group VIP is?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you could only understand the depth of my mercy, you’d be moved. So moved that you’ll get wet between your thighs.” Ryuuen laughed, as though such vulgar language was funny.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida Kikyou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The name dropped cold — known since the second day of the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I’ve known Kushida was the VIP since the second day of the test,” Ryuuen said.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just felt so sorry for you. You were oh-so-incredibly confident in your victory that you looked down on others. You were desperate to get your stories straight, assuming no one would get the answer right. That’s why I went along with it until the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata’s “How did you figure it out?” carries curiosity and fear; the answer names Horikita, not him.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, the answer to that… Well, it involves you, Suzune,” answered Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I figured it out because of your body. The movements of your eyes and mouth. Your breathing. Your behavior. Your tone. Everything about you told me that you were lying,” continued Ryuuen in an eerie voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Body-language read of Horikita’s lie — the method that beat the VIP secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jokes? If it’s a joke, then how do I know the truth?”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand how you feel. You don’t want to admit that you’re the most incompetent person in the group. But don’t beat yourself up, Suzune. You merely chose the wrong opponent. Besides, this exam was supposed to be pure chaos. At any rate, Class A is in for an especially rude awakening. Relax.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ll understand soon enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The four simultaneous betrayal emails — Rat, Horse, Monkey, Rooster answered correctly; he played a major part; Class A VIP list on his screen for Rat, Rooster and Pig.<span class=\"pg\">p.240-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t this great, Suzune? Thanks to your blunder, the Dragon group managed to clear this test with Outcome #1. Because of that, all the classes should receive a boost in points,” Ryuuen crowed. He clapped his hands and wore a satisfied grin. “If you beg for it, I’ll tell you the answer. How about it?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ooh, that look you have. It’s pretty sexy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I made some adjustments and arrived at the root of the test. Then, I just focused on the Class A students,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Cleared without targeting Classes B or D at all — the Class A VIP harvest on one screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry to tell you, Suzune, but you’re my next target. I’m going after you with everything I’ve got. I won’t stop until I tear you to shreds, both in mind and body.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m looking forward to the second semester,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Walks away with his payback for the island — the threat Ayanokōji turns into quiet excitement.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The defensive vote he bent to 1% — named in Ayanokōji’s explanation of Dragon Outcome #1.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
